      {
        "term": "Hypothesis Testing",
        "def": "i. A statistical hypothesis is a statement about the value of a statistic.\nIn statistical inference &quot;accept Ho&quot; means that there is insufficient information to reject Ho\nIf a null hypothesis Ho: = 50 is rejected at 1% level of significance, it will also be rejected a 5% level of significance.\nWhen a true null hypothesis has been rejected, we say that Type-I error might have been committed."
      }
