   "theoryPashto": "(iii)\\ (a)\\quad P\\left(\\frac{1}{4}<X<\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\int_{1/4}^{1/2}f(x)\\,dx=\\int_{1/4}^{1/2}2x\\,dx=2\\int_{1/4}^{1/2}x\\,dx\n\n=2\\left.\\left(\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right)\\right|_{1/4}^{1/2}=\\left.x^2\\right|_{1/4}^{1/2}=\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{16}=\\frac{4-1}{16}=\\frac{3}{16}\n\n(b)\\quad P\\left(X>\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{1}f(x)\\,dx=\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{1}2x\\,dx=2\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{1}x\\,dx=2\\left.\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right|_{1/2}^{1}\n\n=\\left.x^2\\right|_{1/2}^{1}=1-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{4-1}{4}=\\frac{3}{4}\n\n(c) P\\left(X=\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=0، ځکه چې په متصل حالت کې د یوه ټکي احتمال تل له صفر سره برابر وي.\n\n2.3.3 د متصل تصادفي متغیر تمه، واریانس او معیاري انحراف\n\nکه X یو متصل تصادفي متغیر وي، نو د X تمه شوی قیمت E(X)=\\int_x x\\,f(x)\\,dx دی، په دې شرط چې شتون ولري.\n\nبېلګه 2.16\n\nفرض کړئ X یو متصل تصادفي متغیر دی چې pdf یې دا ده\n\n$f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{matrix}\\frac{x}{2} & 0\\le x\\le 2\\\\ 0 & \\textit{otherwise}\\end{matrix}\\right.$\n\nد X منځنی، واریانس او معیاري انحراف پیدا کړئ.\n\nحل:\n\n(i) د تعریف له مخې\n\n\\text{Mean}=E(X)=\\int_x x\\,f(x)\\,dx\n\n=\\int_{0}^{2}x\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)dx=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_{0}^{2}x^2dx=\\frac{1}{2}\\left.\\left(\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right)\\right|_{0}^{2}\n\n=\\left.\\left(\\frac{x^3}{6}\\right)\\right|_{0}^{2}=\\frac{8}{6}-0=\\frac{4}{3}=1.333\n\n(ii) د تعریف له مخې\n\nV(X)=E(X^2)-[E(X)]^2\n\n=\\int_{0}^{2}x^2f(x)\\,dx-\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^2\n\n=\\int_{0}^{2}x^2\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)dx-\\frac{16}{9}\n\n=\\int_{0}^{2}\\frac{x^3}{2}dx-\\frac{16}{9}=\\left.\\frac{x^4}{8}\\right|_{0}^{2}-\\frac{16}{9}=\\left(\\frac{16}{8}-0\\right)-\\frac{16}{9}\n\n=2-1.78=0.22\n\n(iii)\\quad S.D(X)=\\sqrt{0.22}=0.47\n\nبېلګه 2.17\n\nیو تصادفي متغیر X دا کثافت تابع لري\n\n$f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{matrix}(2-2x), & 0\\le x\\le 1\\\\ 0 & \\textit{otherwise}\\end{matrix}\\right.$\n\nپیدا کړئ (i) E(X) (ii) E(X²) (iii) E(2X) (iv) E(2X−1) (v) د X واریانس او معیاري انحراف",
   "content": "<p>(iii)\\ (a)\\quad P\\left(\\frac{1}{4}&lt;X&lt;\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\int_{1/4}^{1/2}f(x)\\,dx=\\int_{1/4}^{1/2}2x\\,dx=2\\int_{1/4}^{1/2}x\\,dx</p><p>=2\\left.\\left(\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right)\\right|_{1/4}^{1/2}=\\left.x^2\\right|_{1/4}^{1/2}=\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{16}=\\frac{4-1}{16}=\\frac{3}{16}</p><p>(b)\\quad P\\left(X&gt;\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{1}f(x)\\,dx=\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{1}2x\\,dx=2\\int_{\\frac{1}{2}}^{1}x\\,dx=2\\left.\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right|_{1/2}^{1}</p><p>=\\left.x^2\\right|_{1/2}^{1}=1-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{4-1}{4}=\\frac{3}{4}</p><p>(c) P\\left(X=\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=0, because in continuous case point probability is always equal to zero.</p><p>2.3.3 Expectation, variance and standard deviation of a continuous random variable</p><p>If X is a continuous random variable, then expected value of X is given by E(X)=\\int_x x\\,f(x)\\,dx, provided that it exists.</p><p>Example 2.16</p><p>Let X be a continuous random variable with pdf given by</p><p>$f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{matrix}\\frac{x}{2} &amp; 0\\le x\\le 2\\\\ 0 &amp; \\textit{otherwise}\\end{matrix}\\right.$</p><p>Find the mean, variance and standard deviation of X.</p><p>Solution:</p><p>(i) By definition</p><p>\\text{Mean}=E(X)=\\int_x x\\,f(x)\\,dx</p><p>=\\int_{0}^{2}x\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)dx=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_{0}^{2}x^2dx=\\frac{1}{2}\\left.\\left(\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right)\\right|_{0}^{2}</p><p>=\\left.\\left(\\frac{x^3}{6}\\right)\\right|_{0}^{2}=\\frac{8}{6}-0=\\frac{4}{3}=1.333</p><p>(ii) By definition</p><p>V(X)=E(X^2)-[E(X)]^2</p><p>=\\int_{0}^{2}x^2f(x)\\,dx-\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^2</p><p>=\\int_{0}^{2}x^2\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)dx-\\frac{16}{9}</p><p>=\\int_{0}^{2}\\frac{x^3}{2}dx-\\frac{16}{9}=\\left.\\frac{x^4}{8}\\right|_{0}^{2}-\\frac{16}{9}=\\left(\\frac{16}{8}-0\\right)-\\frac{16}{9}</p><p>=2-1.78=0.22</p><p>(iii)\\quad S.D(X)=\\sqrt{0.22}=0.47</p><p>Example 2.17</p><p>A random variable X has the density function given by</p><p>$f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{matrix}(2-2x), &amp; 0\\le x\\le 1\\\\ 0 &amp; \\textit{otherwise}\\end{matrix}\\right.$</p><p>Find (i) E(X) (ii) E(X²) (iii) E(2X) (iv) E(2X−1) (v) variance and standard deviation of X</p>",
