   "content": "<p>2.7 Define probability distribution, probability function and probability density function. What are the two basic properties of all probability functions?</p><p>2.8 Find probability distribution for the number of heads when 2 balanced coins are tossed.</p><p>2.9 In a family of three children find the probability distribution for the number of girls.</p><p>2.10 A random variable has the following probability distribution.</p><p>(i) Find the value of c. (ii) P(X&lt;7) (iii) P(X\\ge 6)</p><p>2.11 A coin is tossed three times in succession. Find the probability distribution for the number of heads minus number of tails.</p><p>2.12 A pair of fair dice is rolled once. Find the probability distribution for the difference of dots.</p><p>2.13 Check whether the following is a probability distribution or not? If not, then why?</p><p>2.14 A discrete random variable has the probability mass function:</p><p>$p(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{matrix}\\frac{{}^{3}_{x}C}{8}, &amp; x=0,1,2,3\\\\ 0, &amp; \\textit{elsewhere}\\end{matrix}\\right.$</p><p>Find (i) P(X=2) (ii) P(X&gt;1) (iii) P(0&lt;X&lt;3)</p><p>2.15 (a) Define p.d.f and state its properties. (b) The density function of a continuous random variable X is:</p><p>$f(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}Ax^2, &amp; 0\\le x\\le 1\\\\ 0, &amp; \\textit{elsewhere}\\end{bmatrix}$</p><p>Find (i) value of the constant A (ii) P(X\\le 0.5) (ii) P(0.2&lt;X&lt;0.3).</p><p>2.16 Discuss mathematical expectation. Write some of its important properties.</p><p>2.17 For the following discrete probability distribution of X</p><p>Find (i) E(X) (ii) E(X²) (iii) E(2X+5)</p><p>2.18 Find the mean, variance and standard deviation for the following probability distribution:</p><p>2.19 Let Y be a random variable with probability distribution as follows:</p><p>Find (i) Expected value</p><p>(ii) Variance</p><p>(iii) S.D for the random variable Y</p><p>2.20 A variable X has the p.d.f f(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}kx^3(1-x), &amp; 0\\le x\\le 1\\\\ 0, &amp; \\textit{otherwise}\\end{bmatrix}</p><p>Find (i) The value of k (ii) E(X) (iii) Variance (iv) S.D</p>",
