   "content": "<p>Example 3.22</p><p>A bowl contains 4 green and 7 red balls. A sample of 5 balls is selected from the bowl without replacement. Find the probability distribution for the number of green balls. Compute the mean and variance of this probability distribution and compare them with the theoretical mean and variance.</p><p>Solution:</p><p>The bowl contains</p><p>Here n=5</p><p>X: number of green balls selected</p><p>X=0,1,2,3,4. [5 is not possible as there are only 4 green balls.].</p><p>$\\therefore p(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{matrix}\\dfrac{\\binom{4}{x}\\binom{11-4}{5-x}}{\\binom{11}{5}}, &amp; x=0,1,2,3,4\\\\ 0 &amp; \\textit{otherwise}\\end{matrix}\\right.$</p><p>Now hypergeometric probability distribution of X is given as</p>",
