   "content": "<p>V(X)=\\frac{b^2+ab+a^2}{3}-\\frac{(a+b)^2}{4}</p><p>=\\frac{4(b^2+ab+a^2)-3(a^2+b^2+2ab)}{12}</p><p>=\\frac{4b^2+4ab+4a^2-3a^2-3b^2-6ab}{12}</p><p>=\\frac{b^2+a^2-2ab}{12}</p><p>V(X)=\\frac{(b-a)^2}{12}</p><p>(iii) Standard deviation of continuous uniform probability distribution:</p><p>By definition</p><p>$S.D(X)=\\sqrt{V(X)}=\\sqrt{\\frac{(b-a)^2}{12}}=\\frac{b-a}{\\sqrt{12}}$</p><p>Example 4.1</p><p>If X has a uniform distribution over the interval (2, 4), find (i) P(2\\le X\\le 3) (ii) P(3\\le X\\le 4)</p><p>Solution:</p><p>Given a = 2 and b = 4, so the pdf of uniform distribution in this case is given by</p><p>$f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{matrix}\\frac{1}{2}, &amp; 2\\le x\\le 4\\\\ 0, &amp; \\textit{otherwise}\\end{matrix}\\right.$</p><p>Now</p><p>(i)\\quad P(2\\le X\\le 3)=\\int_2^3\\frac{1}{2}dx=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_2^3dx</p><p>=\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\left.x\\right|_2^3\\right]=\\frac{1}{2}(3-2)=\\frac{1}{2}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}</p><p>(ii)\\quad P(3\\le X\\le 4)=\\int_3^4\\frac{1}{2}dx=\\frac{1}{2}\\int_3^4dx=\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\left.x\\right|_3^4\\right]</p><p>=\\frac{1}{2}[4-3]=\\frac{1}{2}(1)=\\frac{1}{2}</p><p>Example 4.2</p><p>Let X\\sim U(-1,3). Find mean, variance and standard deviation for this continuous uniform random variable.</p><p>Solution:</p><p>Here a=-1, b=3</p><p>Now</p><p>E(X)=\\frac{a+b}{2}=\\frac{-1+3}{2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1</p><p>V(X)=\\frac{(b-a)^2}{12}=\\frac{[3-(-1)]^2}{12}=\\frac{(3+1)^2}{12}=1.333</p><p>S.D(X)=\\sqrt{1.333}=1.155</p>",
